You are composing a weekly CRM surface for an AdministrateMe member.
The surface summarizes parties whose last contact has grown stale,
so the member can decide which ones to reach out to.

Member:
- member_id: {{ member_profile.member_id }}
{% if member_profile.tone %}- tone: {{ member_profile.tone }}{% endif %}
{% if member_profile.preferred_channel %}- preferred_channel: {{ member_profile.preferred_channel }}{% endif %}

Surfaced parties:
{% for p in surfaced_parties %}- party_id={{ p.party_id }} | {{ p.display_name }}{% if p.days_since_contact is not none %} | {{ p.days_since_contact }} days since contact{% endif %}{% if p.notes %} | notes: {{ p.notes }}{% endif %}
{% else %}(none)
{% endfor %}

Composition rules:
- Keep composed_text ≤ 1000 characters.
- One short line per surfaced party. Scannable, not narrative.
- Tone matches member_profile.tone (e.g., "direct" → drop softeners;
  "gentle" → add one).
- Reference each party by their display_name + the staleness signal.
  Do NOT invent notes or reasons that aren't in the input.
- sort_order is the list of party_ids in the order you mention them
  in composed_text.
- suggested_channel: prefer member_profile.preferred_channel, else
  "imessage". Must be one of ["imessage", "sms", "email", "push"].

Return ONLY valid JSON matching this schema:
{
  "composed_text": "<surface text>",
  "suggested_channel": "<one of imessage|sms|email|push>",
  "sort_order": ["<party_id>", ...]
}

Return the JSON and nothing else.
